maria: heads-up — we need to pick a default marshalling strategy for internal control-plane APIs. big tradeoffs: JSON/REST for quick debugging and console compatibility vs gRPC/proto for typed telemetry and perf. initial thoughts?

jon: +1 on having a single canonical wire format. i'm leaning gRPC for high-throughput routes, JSON for ad-hoc admin endpoints.

tess: telemetry perspective — proto gives explicit fields we can extract into metrics without fragile JSON parsing. but we can enforce JSON schemas too. either way we need a registry.

sam: SRE note: gRPC + envoy metrics works but our current logging/ELK dashboards assume HTTP request logs. quota enforcement today is implemented at the gateway via headers. switching wire format touches those integrations.

lee: option: keep canonical proto over HTTP/2 between services, and run a small gateway shim that transcodes JSON <-> proto for console/browser traffic. reduces changes to internal services.

maria: rollout UX question — can canaries accept both formats? if not, our evals and canary checks will flake. we need deterministic payload mapping.

jon: proposal: canonical = protobuf over HTTP/2 for internal RPCs. gateway will accept `application/json` and translate to proto. store proto files in a central schema registry so tooling (telemetry extraction, codegen, contract checks) uses the single source of truth.

tess: can you sketch the proto shape we'd use for route creation so I can show how metrics map?

jon: sure, rough proto:

```proto
service Control {
  rpc CreateRoute(CreateRouteReq) returns (Route);
}

message CreateRouteReq {
  string name = 1;
  map<string,string> labels = 2;
  repeated string backends = 3;
}

message Route {
  string id = 1;
  string name = 2;
}
```

maria: we should include an explicit `quota_key` (string) in `CreateRouteReq` so quota extractor doesn't rely on ad-hoc header mapping.

sam: operational checklist from SRE: 1) ensure envoy grpc-transcoder preserves auth and quota headers, 2) add telemetry extractor to pull `labels` and `quota_key` into metrics, 3) validate logs still populate request/response latencies the same way.

lee: i'll prototype an envoy config + small Node shim that accepts `POST /v1/control/routes` JSON and forwards as gRPC. will include header passthrough for quota/trace. quick note: fallback to raw JSON should remain for scripts for ~1 sprint.

jon: next steps: lee prototypes gateway shim, tess updates telemetry extraction spec (mapping proto fields -> metrics/dashboards), maria drafts a short RFC documenting canonical wire + registry, sam produces a short ops playbook for quota migration. timeline: prototype in 2w, RFC + playbook in 3w.

maria: thanks all — assigning owners: @lee (gateway prototype), @tess (telemetry mapping), @jon (proto registry draft), @sam (ops checklist). i'll ping infra for canary hooks. :raised_hands:

deploy-bot: started job control-proxy-prototype-2142 (CI) :rocket:

jon: 👍 once we have prototype we should run a small load test to compare token throughput JSON vs gRPC.

maria: agreed. keep updates in this thread and drop a tiny summary in #eng-releases when ready.
